Subject: [PATCH] core: add the Sega Chihiro machine

This records the XGrid integration of the Sega Chihiro machine. The machine
itself is the ported xemu-Playtest-v2 / XPSemu-Chihiro source under
xemu/hw/xbox/chihiro/ (LGPL-2.0-or-later; chihiro-pic.* LGPL-2.1-or-later;
chihiro-des.* BSD-3-Clause). The memory-backed block driver is
xemu/block/blkmemory.c with xemu/include/block/blkmemory.h (GPL-2.0-or-later).

New files (whole files, not shown as hunks):
  block/blkmemory.c
  include/block/blkmemory.h
  hw/xbox/chihiro/*.c, *.h and meson.build

The diff below covers the edits to the existing xemu tree, including the OHCI
enumeration hooks, the keyboard/gamepad/mouse JVS mapping, player 1's pointer
aim, player 2's second-pad/arrow aim, both card readers, the gun-profile menu
suppression, the gamepad force-feedback output, the steering-wheel SDL haptic
effects, Windows Raw Input, Linux evdev and macOS IOHID per-device light-gun
input, the IOKit/CoreFoundation link for macOS, and the JVS analog diagnostic.
It applies on top of the XGrid 0.8.139 tree with patches 0001-0017.
